Gears of War 3: keep DLSS/FSR from warping the HUD, subtitles and chapter titles. Every draw after the
full-screen tonemap pass (a small full-screen draw sampling one of the frame's full-size colour resolves) is UI;
its screen rectangle is estimated by running its vertex shader on the CPU
(DrawExtentEstimator::EstimateVertexBounds), only for small draws and at most 64 a frame. The rectangles become
an R8 mask: zero camera motion there, DLSS bias-current-colour mask, FSR reactive mask. gow2_ui_mask (default
true) turns it off. Written by Gemini 4 Argon (Antigravity CLI) from a brief, reviewed and adjusted.

